{"description":"Importing a `cmt:` unit is refused unconditionally: `isKnownStateDomain` and `Unit.StateVectorValue` in `exchange/import.go` do not know the `note-state` domain, so any comment unit with an execution/content state change-log entry fails with `import refused: unit ... change-log entry N uses unknown domain \"note-state\"`. Found while building the provenance round-trip fixtures; the exchange fixtures contain no `cmt` unit, so no test reaches it.","impact":"Comment units cannot be exchanged at all, which means a package containing notes — the normal output of a capture-heavy repository — is rejected wholesale rather than partially. The failure is also late and misleading: it reports an unknown state domain rather than an unhandled artifact type.","acceptanceCriteria":"- `cmt:` units survive export -\u003e import -\u003e export byte-identically.\n- A note-state change-log entry is accepted by both `isKnownStateDomain` and `StateVectorValue`.\n- A fixture covering a package that contains at least one comment unit exists in `exchange/testdata`."}